{"causes": ["His father, Marcus Tullius Cicero, instilled in him a strong sense of civic duty and provided him with a comprehensive education in rhetoric and philosophy.", "The assassination of Julius Caesar in 44 BCE plunged Rome into renewed civil war, forcing Cicero Minor to choose sides in the conflict between the Liberators and the Second Triumvirate.", "The eventual triumph of Octavian (Augustus) and his policy of reconciliation allowed Cicero Minor to return from exile and pursue a distinguished career within the new political order."], "effects": ["Cicero Minor's proconsulship of Syria from 27-25 BCE contributed to the pacification and stability of Rome's eastern frontier during the early years of the Augustan Principate.", "His successful suppression of local rebellions in Syria demonstrated the administrative and military effectiveness of the nascent Roman Empire under Augustus.", "His career provided a living link to the memory of his father, Marcus Tullius Cicero, maintaining a connection to the ideals of the Republic even as the Principate took hold."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "marcus-tullius-cicero", "sourceName": "Marcus Tullius Cicero", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "cicero-minor", "targetName": "Cicero Minor", "context": "Marcus Tullius Cicero, as his father, profoundly influenced Cicero Minor's education and early political leanings towards the Republican cause."}, {"sourceSlug": "cicero-minor", "sourceName": "Cicero Minor", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-philippi", "targetName": "Battle of Philippi", "context": "Cicero Minor commanded a cavalry detachment in Brutus's army during the decisive Battle of Philippi in 42 BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "cicero-minor", "sourceName": "Cicero Minor", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "syria-roman-province", "targetName": "Syria, Roman Province", "context": "Cicero Minor served as the Roman Proconsul of Syria from 27 to 25 BCE, overseeing its administration and military affairs.